## Phase 1: Full System Design  

Johnston Engineering estimates an engineering design labor cost of $42,600 USD for Phase 1. This phase of the project will solidify requirements, propose, iterate and finalize system design for GE review and approval before moving to Phase 2.

## Phase 2: Fabrication, Verification, and Delivery

Johnston Engineering estimates fabrication and verification labor and hardware and delivery costs to total $56,000 USD for Phase 2**.**** ** This phase of the project will create drawings and the Bill of Materials (BOM), order hardware, fabricate components, inspect hardware, assemble system, perform testing, and ship the system to GE Aerospace. Hardware procurement and fabrication labor and material costs are estimated at $29,900. Assembly labor and delivery costs are estimated at $26,1000 (assuming ~$3,000 in shipping charges). 

# Project Timeline

The complete project duration is 86 workdays assuming one staff per labor category. If the project kicks off in August 2025, **Phase****s 1**** ****&****2**** are ****scheduled**** for completion by ****11****/****30****/2025****.** 

Johnston Engineering has the capacity to add staff to the project to complete the work on a faster timeline if preferred. JE estimates we can complete the work by 10/31/2025 with additional staff and estimates an price increase of ~10% due to additional staff in meetings etc. 

